WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:05.660
The war that ended the world started on October
9th, 1971.

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:10.760
Tensions had been brewing for years between
America and the Soviet Union, and even though

00:00:10.760 --> 00:00:15.290
people had done their best to keep a sense
of normalcy, everyone was wondering when the

00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:19.830
Cold War that had been brewing for the past
30 years would boil over.

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:24.090
There were those who had been preparing for
it for years, while others assumed that it

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.779
would never amount to anything.

00:00:25.779 --> 00:00:31.460
Neither nation wanted to make the first nuclear
strike, and even if that happened, the engineers

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:34.700
would come out of their underground cities
to intervene.

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:39.540
But nobody knew for sure if the two world
superpowers could ever come to an agreement,

00:00:39.540 --> 00:00:42.840
or if it would all end in total destruction.

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:47.370
October 9th was the day that question was
answered.

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:52.230
The first American nuclear warhead detonated
over the Gulf of Finland, only a few miles

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:57.559
away from the city of Leningrad, where people
were going about their day blissfully unaware

00:00:57.559 --> 00:01:00.670
of the destruction that was about to befall
them.

00:01:00.670 --> 00:01:06.400
First came a city-wide blackout as the power
grid was bombarded with a huge surge of radiation

00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:11.430
that caused bulbs to blow and wires to glow
like they'd been struck by lightning.

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:16.860
There was barely any time to react before
the next wave hit- a white-hot flash so bright

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:20.550
that many of those who couldn't get to cover
were blinded.

00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:26.590
The third wave, by far the most destructive,
was the force of the explosion itself.

00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:31.840
Like a powerful burning wind, it swept through
the city, breaking windows, knocking over

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:37.500
streetlights, ripping the leaves off of trees,
and bathing every car, building, and person

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:38.890
with ash.

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:42.660
People are trapped under the debris as some
of the city's older, less well-maintained

00:01:42.660 --> 00:01:45.049
buildings come crumbling down.

00:01:45.049 --> 00:01:48.939
Even though the Soviet government had been
preparing for this day to come and the Russian

00:01:48.939 --> 00:01:53.860
people had been put through mandatory safety
drills, no amount of practice or planning

00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:56.229
could've prepared them for the real thing.

00:01:56.229 --> 00:02:00.939
The streets erupted into chaos- cars were
crashing into buildings, either because their

00:02:00.939 --> 00:02:05.400
drivers had been blinded by the light of the
distant explosion or because the initial wave

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:08.229
of radiation had shorted the batteries.

00:02:08.229 --> 00:02:12.200
People nearly trampled each other trying to
get to underground shelters as police and

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:15.640
military tried to yell directions over the
cacophony.

00:02:15.640 --> 00:02:18.810
Among the crowd, a family desperately tried
to stay together.

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:24.110
Irina and Nikolai Belitrov held tight to their
children, Alexei and Tatiana.

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:28.410
The whole family was still in their pajamas
and barely had time to get their shoes on

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:32.550
before they started rushing towards the neighborhood's
designated underground bunker.

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:37.720
Irina had Tatiana, who was only two, clutched
tight to her chest, and Nikolai tried his

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:43.220
best to keep ten-year-old Alexei's eyes shielded
as they walked past the dead bodies of people

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:45.300
who were once their friends and neighbors.

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:50.610
“It'll be alright soon, son,” Nikolai
said, as much to try and convince himself

00:02:50.610 --> 00:02:55.000
as his son, “We're going underground, just
like in the safety drills.”

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:58.019
Alexei nodded solemnly and kept his gaze straight
ahead.

00:02:58.019 --> 00:03:01.720
They were almost at the end of the street,
when just above the sounds of air raid sirens

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:05.409
and screaming people, Alexei heard a familiar
voice.

00:03:05.409 --> 00:03:06.459
“Alexei!

00:03:06.459 --> 00:03:07.510
Alexei!”

00:03:07.510 --> 00:03:12.049
The boy looked down to see his teacher, Mr.
Petrov, trapped in the wreckage of his car.

00:03:12.049 --> 00:03:14.879
He must've been driving to work when the bomb
struck.

00:03:14.879 --> 00:03:16.319
“Father, stop!”

00:03:16.319 --> 00:03:18.700
Alexei yelled, tugging at his father's shirt
sleeve.

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:22.831
“That's my teacher, we have to help him,
or he won't make it to the shelter.”

00:03:22.831 --> 00:03:26.769
“The soldiers will help him once everyone
else is in,” said Nikolai.

00:03:26.769 --> 00:03:27.769
Alexei didn't listen.

00:03:27.769 --> 00:03:31.460
He wriggled free of his father's grip and
ran to where his teacher lay pinned under

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:32.730
the wrecked vehicle.

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:37.940
Nikolai was calling after him, and though
Irina wanted to wait for Alexei to come back,

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:41.930
she was swept up in the tide of people and
separated from her husband.

00:03:41.930 --> 00:03:45.349
Mr. Petrov was crying, thanking Alexei for
coming to his aid.

00:03:45.349 --> 00:03:49.710
As Alexei got closer, he saw there was blood
pooling out from under the wreck- it seemed

00:03:49.710 --> 00:03:54.880
if Mr. Petrov were going to make it out his
legs would likely be badly damaged.

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:59.290
Alexei tried to lift the car himself, but
even though he was strong for his age, he

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:01.230
was still only a child.

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:04.500
A soldier who had been helping people into
the bomb shelter stopped what he was doing

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:06.170
and ran over to Alexei.

00:04:06.170 --> 00:04:07.170
“Hey, kid!”

00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:08.170
the soldier shouted.

00:04:08.170 --> 00:04:12.610
“Leave him alone and go back to your family-
you're going to hurt yourself.”

00:04:12.610 --> 00:04:16.639
Alexei kicked and struggled against the soldier's
grip as he was dragged back into the line

00:04:16.639 --> 00:04:17.639
with his family.

00:04:17.639 --> 00:04:19.350
“But he's in trouble!”

00:04:19.350 --> 00:04:20.350
Alexei cried.

00:04:20.350 --> 00:04:25.220
“It's not your job to save him,” his father
scolded as he took his hand and led him down

00:04:25.220 --> 00:04:28.949
the stairs where they would rejoin his mother
and sister.

00:04:28.949 --> 00:04:33.580
As Alexei and his father descended into the
tunnels, Alexei heard a gunshot from the street

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:34.580
above.

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:39.270
Though he would survive long after that day,
he never saw his teacher Mr. Petrov again.

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:42.350
He never asked his father about what happened.

00:04:42.350 --> 00:04:47.350
The Belitrov family was reunited in the underground
shelter, which had once been an underground

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:48.639
train station.

00:04:48.639 --> 00:04:53.400
Tatiana had started crying, and Nikolai tried
desperately to quiet her.

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:58.170
Irina hugged her son so tight he felt she
might squeeze the life out of him.

00:04:58.170 --> 00:05:03.919
They were packed in with a dozen other families,
some that they knew and others who were strangers.

00:05:03.919 --> 00:05:07.960
Alexei recognized some of the other children
from school, and he saw that some were there

00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:09.449
without their parents.

00:05:09.449 --> 00:05:13.009
While they were in the station, a soldier
addressed the group and explained what would

00:05:13.009 --> 00:05:14.139
happen next.

00:05:14.139 --> 00:05:18.830
The train station was to serve as their temporary
shelter until the proper negotiations were

00:05:18.830 --> 00:05:20.630
made with the engineers.

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:25.139
As per a treaty that had been written and
signed after the second world war, the engineers

00:05:25.139 --> 00:05:30.449
had agreed to open the borders of their underground
civilization to humans fleeing from a crisis

00:05:30.449 --> 00:05:31.600
above ground.

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:36.380
Once the government had made a decision, the
survivors were to be taken deep underground,

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:38.800
where they would live until the war was over.

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:43.010
Above ground, the Soviet Union began dealing
with the fallout of the initial attack.

00:05:43.010 --> 00:05:47.770
It was clear that America could no longer
be dealt with reasonably if they were willing

00:05:47.770 --> 00:05:50.800
to bomb one of the USSR's biggest cities.

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:55.389
Though the bombing had cut communications
between Leningrad and Moscow, eventually,

00:05:55.389 --> 00:05:59.840
contact was re-established, and the army was
able to radio the Kremlin with a full report

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:01.130
on the damage.

00:06:01.130 --> 00:06:06.280
Leningrad was in ruin, with over a third of
the population dead or otherwise too wounded

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:08.160
to move underground.

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:12.470
Those who had made it underground were receiving
treatment for everything from broken bones

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:14.630
and blindness to radiation poisoning.

00:06:14.630 --> 00:06:17.770
In a word, it was chaos.

00:06:17.770 --> 00:06:21.700
Russian parliament was quick and ruthless
in their decision to strike back.

00:06:21.700 --> 00:06:26.479
On October 12th, Secretary Brezhnev authorized
nuclear missiles to be launched at both New

00:06:26.479 --> 00:06:29.130
York City and Washington DC.

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:34.990
Millions were killed, and just like in Russia,
the survivors retreated underground.

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:39.211
America didn't go down without a fight, though,
and launched another missile attack, this

00:06:39.211 --> 00:06:41.110
time at Moscow.

00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:45.319
It wasn't long before both countries' allies
were involved in the conflict as well, with

00:06:45.319 --> 00:06:50.940
missile strikes coming from France, China,
North Korea, Germany, and the United Kingdom.

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:55.900
Within a month, the surface of the Earth was
dangerously irradiated, and any humans who

00:06:55.900 --> 00:06:58.240
were still living had retreated underground.

00:06:58.240 --> 00:07:02.900
But though the world had ended, the war hadn't.

00:07:02.900 --> 00:07:07.380
Alexei Belitrov and his family struggled to
adjust to their new life underground.

00:07:07.380 --> 00:07:11.759
Though the engineers were intelligent and
human-like, their world was so different from

00:07:11.759 --> 00:07:15.690
the world Alexei had lived in for the first
10 years of his life.

00:07:15.690 --> 00:07:21.020
He barely ever saw them- the engineers were
nocturnal, sleeping while an artificial sun

00:07:21.020 --> 00:07:25.310
nourished the genetically-engineered plants
that grew around the city.

00:07:25.310 --> 00:07:30.370
But any time he tried to ask questions about
them, he was met with hushed silence by the

00:07:30.370 --> 00:07:31.370
adults.

00:07:31.370 --> 00:07:36.199
The engineers were spoken of in hushed, almost
reverent tones- they were the beings that

00:07:36.199 --> 00:07:41.539
saved humanity, yes, but they had also helped
build the weapons that led to the war in the

00:07:41.539 --> 00:07:42.840
first place.

00:07:42.840 --> 00:07:46.909
Alexei barely had any time to settle into
this new life before what remained of the

00:07:46.909 --> 00:07:50.139
Russian army started looking for new recruits.

00:07:50.139 --> 00:07:54.360
Reports had come in from an above-ground scout
that the Americans were working on a new type

00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:59.199
of armor that could fully shield the wearer
against radiation, and the Soviets couldn't

00:07:59.199 --> 00:08:04.360
afford to be outmatched when their army was
still recovering from multiple nuclear attacks.

00:08:04.360 --> 00:08:09.940
But the army wasn't asking for able-bodied
adult men to enlist- they were looking for

00:08:09.940 --> 00:08:10.940
children.

00:08:10.940 --> 00:08:14.550
“We can't possibly send our son to war,”
Irina said.

00:08:14.550 --> 00:08:17.740
Arguments at the dinner table had become common
in the Belitrov family.

00:08:17.740 --> 00:08:21.270
“He wouldn't be going to war,” Nikolai
argued.

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:25.150
“Not until their new anti-radiation technology
is perfected.

00:08:25.150 --> 00:08:26.940
He won't be ready until he's an adult.”

00:08:26.940 --> 00:08:30.960
“How do you know that what they're making
in those labs won't kill him?”

00:08:30.960 --> 00:08:31.960
Irina said.

00:08:31.960 --> 00:08:35.260
“Do we really want to trust these underground
devils with our son?

00:08:35.260 --> 00:08:38.870
How much do we really know about the engineers,
anyway?”

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:44.720
“They could've let us all burn on the surface,”
Nikolai said, “but they didn't.

00:08:44.720 --> 00:08:46.560
I think we should trust them.”

00:08:46.560 --> 00:08:48.800
“I want to go,” said Alexei.

00:08:48.800 --> 00:08:49.800
“I should.

00:08:49.800 --> 00:08:51.950
Some of my friends have already enlisted.”

00:08:51.950 --> 00:08:55.680
Both of his parents were stunned, but it made
sense to Alexei.

00:08:55.680 --> 00:08:59.630
He wanted the war to be over, and he wanted
to leave the underground city.

00:08:59.630 --> 00:09:04.660
But most importantly, he wanted to know if
anyone was still alive on the surface.

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:09.660
If there was even a sliver of a chance that
it could be habitable again, he wanted to

00:09:09.660 --> 00:09:11.010
find out.

00:09:11.010 --> 00:09:16.820
After much discussion, Irina and Nikolai agreed-
it was what was best for the future of Russia,

00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:20.570
and, ultimately, the future of the human race.

00:09:20.570 --> 00:09:24.470
Alexei's parents delivered him to the office
of army recruitment, and he was taken by a

00:09:24.470 --> 00:09:28.970
man named Commander Volkov to a specialized
research facility.

00:09:28.970 --> 00:09:32.339
This was when Alexei met an engineer for the
first time.

00:09:32.339 --> 00:09:37.290
The engineer was tall and hairy, like a bear
walking on its back legs, but with a face

00:09:37.290 --> 00:09:39.300
and hands more like a human's.

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:43.810
It was overseeing a group of humans and other
engineers as they tinkered with machines that

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:46.769
Alexei couldn't even begin to guess the purpose
of.

00:09:46.769 --> 00:09:50.480
“Don't be frightened, Alexei,” Commander
Volkov said.

00:09:50.480 --> 00:09:55.920
“They're going to explain the procedure
to you before you have to agree to anything.”

00:09:55.920 --> 00:09:59.990
The engineer looked the boy over, then held
up a jar containing something that looked

00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:01.930
like an insect's exoskeleton.

00:10:01.930 --> 00:10:06.620
It was green, the same shade as the USSR's
army uniforms.

00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:12.839
“This is our new bio-organic armor prototype,”
the engineer said.

00:10:12.839 --> 00:10:17.540
“We can only graft it onto you while you're
still growing.

00:10:17.540 --> 00:10:25.170
It must grow with you, starting on your back,
then moving to your limbs, then your head.”

00:10:25.170 --> 00:10:28.760
Alexei was frightened by the idea but didn't
want to seem weak.

00:10:28.760 --> 00:10:31.860
He wanted to make sure his father would be
proud of him.

00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:36.280
He was taken into surgery, where the team
of engineers and human doctors grafted the

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:39.560
plate of bio-organic armor onto his spine.

00:10:39.560 --> 00:10:44.459
Once the surgery was over, he was wheeled
into a recovery room, where he was fed a simple

00:10:44.459 --> 00:10:47.459
meal alongside all of his friends and classmates.

00:10:47.459 --> 00:10:50.890
They'd all gone through the same procedure.

00:10:50.890 --> 00:10:55.149
Over the next eight years, Alexei and his
comrades went through the painful process

00:10:55.149 --> 00:10:57.660
of growing their exoskeleton.

00:10:57.660 --> 00:11:03.070
Like the engineer had said, it grew with them,
but the growth happened in painful spurts

00:11:03.070 --> 00:11:04.760
rather than gradually.

00:11:04.760 --> 00:11:07.500
The worst thing about the armor was that it
couldn't be removed.

00:11:07.500 --> 00:11:11.990
But it gave them many advantages to normal
soldiers, as well.

00:11:11.990 --> 00:11:16.120
Once it covered Alexei's legs, he found he
could jump higher and run farther than any

00:11:16.120 --> 00:11:17.370
human normally could.

00:11:17.370 --> 00:11:21.040
When it grew over his arms, it gave him increased
strength.

00:11:21.040 --> 00:11:26.490
By the time he was eighteen, it had covered
his head, giving it a fly-like appearance

00:11:26.490 --> 00:11:31.230
but also granting him stereoscopic vision
and the ability to hear radio transmissions

00:11:31.230 --> 00:11:34.810
without the need for any other communication
device.

00:11:34.810 --> 00:11:39.269
During this time, he and the other boys were
trained by Commander Volkov, learning how

00:11:39.269 --> 00:11:43.959
to use the powers granted to them by their
exoskeletons for combat.

00:11:43.959 --> 00:11:48.850
When they were deemed ready, they were all
outfitted with shoulder cannons, supply packs,

00:11:48.850 --> 00:11:52.741
and guns, all of which were also bio-organic
and were surgically attached.

00:11:52.741 --> 00:11:58.880
It had been eight long years since the end
of the world, and Alexei was now able to set

00:11:58.880 --> 00:12:01.520
foot back on the surface.

00:12:01.520 --> 00:12:07.160
The world he returned to was almost unrecognizable-
there were no signs of life outside of weeds

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:11.149
and vines overtaking the irradiated ruins
of buildings.

00:12:11.149 --> 00:12:16.420
Within the first hour of returning to the
surface, Alexei gave up any hope of finding

00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:17.420
survivors.

00:12:17.420 --> 00:12:21.610
He heard Volkov's voice barking orders through
the suit- there was no time to reminisce about

00:12:21.610 --> 00:12:22.690
the past.

00:12:22.690 --> 00:12:25.540
The soldiers had a job to do.

